WEBVTT

01:42.018 --> 01:46.940
PEELING BACK THE LAYERS

01:55.240 --> 01:56.241
Can I help you?

01:57.033 --> 01:58.827
I'm from Horns Research.

02:16.261 --> 02:17.262
Right this way.

02:26.020 --> 02:27.355
Laboratory Head Deshico?

02:27.856 --> 02:30.483
I'm Gamo from Horns Research.

02:31.442 --> 02:32.318
What do you want?

02:33.111 --> 02:34.112
Is it urgent?

02:34.612 --> 02:36.406
It's a matter of life and death.

02:37.365 --> 02:41.077
I'm sure you're aware that incidents
involving carnivores are on the rise.

02:41.703 --> 02:42.537
I am.

02:43.037 --> 02:46.875
We believe the cause
may be an ingredient in Kines.

02:51.045 --> 02:54.424
Myosin, actin, and myogen were detected.

02:55.508 --> 02:56.885
Those are meat proteins.

02:56.968 --> 03:01.848
Yes. We'd never have guessed
that they'd be found in an energy drink.

03:02.640 --> 03:07.061
However, the amounts are too minute
to cause a reaction to meat consumption.

03:07.812 --> 03:11.774
Thus, we believe it's reacting
to something inside carnivores

03:11.858 --> 03:14.485
and interrupting their nervous systems.

03:14.569 --> 03:15.862
Have you found anything?

03:16.404 --> 03:17.530
Yes.

03:17.614 --> 03:19.324
Your research report.

03:19.407 --> 03:21.576
Oh, you read it?

03:21.659 --> 03:25.496
I did. However, I found your conclusion
a bit hard to believe.

03:28.333 --> 03:29.667
Of course you did.

03:31.210 --> 03:32.921
Mind if I take look at that Kines?

03:33.713 --> 03:34.756
Please.

03:38.718 --> 03:40.136
So...

03:40.220 --> 03:43.139
This is from a normal carnivore.

03:43.973 --> 03:46.559
We'll add a drop of Kines.

03:49.395 --> 03:52.190
No real change.

03:52.857 --> 03:53.733
Right.

03:53.816 --> 03:57.278
And then... Yes. This.

03:57.862 --> 04:01.991
This is a sample from a carnivore
that frequently consumes meat.

04:02.575 --> 04:04.911
I'll add a drop of Kines.

04:08.873 --> 04:12.710
When meat is consumed,
the GST stays in the body.

04:13.294 --> 04:18.424
It binds with the components of Kines,
transforms into a fusion protein,

04:18.508 --> 04:21.928
and causes symptoms similar to
having consumed large amounts of meat.

04:22.428 --> 04:27.141
- If we could prevent that--
- What? Why would you stop it?

04:28.268 --> 04:31.396
It's dangerous.
If we don't do something soon...

04:32.897 --> 04:33.815
Hang on.

04:33.898 --> 04:38.653
In this society of ours,
eating meat is forbidden, correct?

04:39.237 --> 04:40.488
Yes.

04:40.571 --> 04:44.033
That means nobody is eating meat.

04:44.117 --> 04:47.829
So even if they do drink Kines,
there shouldn't be any problem.

04:47.912 --> 04:51.291
- But let's be realistic here--
- Oh?

04:51.374 --> 04:56.170
So you'll turn a blind eye to eating meat,
but you won't tolerate Kines?

04:56.254 --> 04:57.505
No, that's...

04:57.588 --> 05:00.717
A double standard
in our coexistent society.

05:00.800 --> 05:04.262
And Kines is the experimental drug
that will bring it to light.

05:04.345 --> 05:05.972
Doesn't that sound fun?

05:06.055 --> 05:08.433
What are you saying? We can't allow this!

05:08.516 --> 05:10.518
You're right. We can't.

05:11.269 --> 05:14.981
Impersonating colleagues
to steal information, that is.

05:15.940 --> 05:18.109
You always did enjoy
a bit of drama, Louis.

05:19.652 --> 05:23.531
You even removed your precious antlers
to get into character!

05:23.614 --> 05:26.117
Now that's a proper actor!

05:27.493 --> 05:32.498
Not to mention that you killed
the Shishi-Gumi boss and took his seat,

05:32.582 --> 05:35.001
becoming their first-ever herbivore boss.

05:35.084 --> 05:36.085
You're wrong.

05:36.627 --> 05:37.670
Pardon me.

05:37.754 --> 05:39.422
Ex-boss.

05:40.757 --> 05:41.758
What's wrong?

05:42.341 --> 05:46.179
I'm not going to expose your identity
to the public or anything.

05:46.262 --> 05:47.263
Then...

05:47.346 --> 05:51.392
Do you know the current boss
of the Shishi-Gumi?

05:51.976 --> 05:52.894
Yes.

05:52.977 --> 05:54.771
And you know that Melon is a mix?

05:55.354 --> 05:56.355
Melon?

05:57.356 --> 05:59.025
Part gazelle, part carnivore.

05:59.108 --> 06:00.151
A leopard.

06:00.860 --> 06:03.112
I knew it.

06:03.196 --> 06:04.363
A mix.

06:05.156 --> 06:09.077
My favorite research topic.

06:10.661 --> 06:14.332
Regardless of gender or species,

06:14.415 --> 06:17.043
it's only natural
to develop feelings for another.

06:17.710 --> 06:20.505
We crave others
precisely because they're different.

06:21.089 --> 06:23.883
As the ex-boss of the Shishi-Gumi,
you should know.

06:24.884 --> 06:27.220
What about mixes are you researching?

06:28.096 --> 06:32.683
Some mixes have extremely heightened
senses and instincts.

06:33.226 --> 06:35.895
They are truly extraordinary.

06:36.979 --> 06:38.439
You mean super senses?

06:39.023 --> 06:40.108
Right.

06:40.191 --> 06:43.986
Some are able to perceive
immeasurably faint sound or light,

06:44.529 --> 06:47.782
while others
have insatiable appetites or sex drives.

06:47.865 --> 06:50.409
Are senses and desires somehow related?

06:50.493 --> 06:53.037
It's only a hypothesis.

06:53.830 --> 06:56.457
But Melon, while having a delicate body,

06:56.541 --> 06:59.544
also possesses a ferocity
beyond that of a lion.

07:00.253 --> 07:03.005
I can't say anything
about his senses, however.

07:04.298 --> 07:06.092
Do you know anything?

07:06.676 --> 07:09.929
No. I've never spoken to him.

07:10.012 --> 07:12.181
Really? Too bad.

07:17.562 --> 07:22.942
<i>It's true. His body is so slight
that a single lion could take him down,</i>

07:23.484 --> 07:27.572
<i>yet his presence is so oppressive
that the lions cower in fear.</i>

07:28.906 --> 07:31.868
<i>Melon. What a creep.</i>

07:36.831 --> 07:39.208
CHLOE

07:40.376 --> 07:41.461
Hello?

07:41.544 --> 07:43.588
<i>Louis? How did it go?</i>

07:44.130 --> 07:45.381
We found the cause.

07:46.382 --> 07:50.303
Kines reacts with the compounds remaining
in the body after consuming meat,

07:50.386 --> 07:52.555
paralyzing the central nervous system.

07:52.638 --> 07:55.766
<i>Then if it's consumed
by someone who has eaten meat,</i>

07:55.850 --> 07:58.436
<i>there's a high likelihood
of them turning violent.</i>

07:58.978 --> 08:00.605
We've got to act quick.

08:00.688 --> 08:04.942
<i>You mean going after the sellers?
That could take a long time.</i>

08:05.735 --> 08:07.111
You're right.

08:09.405 --> 08:10.531
I have an idea.

08:15.077 --> 08:18.998
UDON BEBEBE

08:20.750 --> 08:22.251
I'm sorry.

08:24.295 --> 08:27.089
I truly am sorry.

08:29.592 --> 08:32.386
Finish this off, would you?

08:34.263 --> 08:35.264
Okay.

08:36.182 --> 08:37.350
Thank you.

08:47.610 --> 08:50.154
It's delicious. I'm so glad to be alive.

08:51.822 --> 08:53.574
Say, Legoshi.

08:54.200 --> 08:57.453
If you'd just give me a call,
I'd be happy to make arrangements.

08:57.995 --> 09:00.957
But you can't just bail on work, okay?

09:01.040 --> 09:02.416
I'm sorry.

09:02.500 --> 09:03.876
And what happened, exactly?

09:03.960 --> 09:05.795
You got shot by Watermelon and died?

09:06.295 --> 09:08.673
- His name is Melon.
- It doesn't matter.

09:09.298 --> 09:13.886
After that, you met your dead mother
and came back to life.

09:13.970 --> 09:15.304
Who's going to believe that?

09:15.388 --> 09:17.348
I'm not lying.

09:20.560 --> 09:23.771
Clean the bathroom and ventilation, okay?

09:24.605 --> 09:25.606
Okay.

09:27.733 --> 09:31.571
<i>It's so warm. I've come back to life.</i>

09:34.991 --> 09:38.411
Did you find the Melda?

09:38.494 --> 09:41.247
It was either lost
or carried out of there.

09:42.331 --> 09:45.001
All we have is this mask.

09:45.751 --> 09:51.173
There's no guest list,
and we can't find Melon or Legoshi.

09:51.257 --> 09:55.928
Any possibility that Melon and the wolf
pulled one over on you?

09:56.804 --> 09:58.472
You mean they're a team?

09:58.556 --> 10:00.349
He really was shot, you know.

10:00.433 --> 10:03.644
Did he use large game bullets?

10:18.951 --> 10:21.412
Mr. Yahya, what happened to Melon?

10:22.204 --> 10:25.291
Even I'm still recovering from my injury.

10:25.374 --> 10:27.376
You're unbelievable.

10:28.210 --> 10:29.670
You've got some will to live.

10:29.754 --> 10:32.381
I'm Gosha's grandson, after all.

10:32.923 --> 10:34.634
Oh, sorry to interrupt.

10:34.717 --> 10:36.969
- I'll come back later.
- It's okay.

10:37.053 --> 10:40.556
This is my partner
in the Melon investigation, Corne.

10:41.349 --> 10:45.603
From one scarred face to another,
nice to meet ya.

10:45.686 --> 10:48.105
The pleasure is mine.

10:49.148 --> 10:50.900
Melon got away.

10:52.193 --> 10:55.529
I'm sorry. I had him in my sights.

10:55.613 --> 10:56.614
No.

10:57.365 --> 11:01.160
It was my mistake
getting a civilian involved.

11:01.786 --> 11:04.205
I put your life in danger.

11:04.288 --> 11:05.998
- Forgive me.
- No.

11:06.082 --> 11:08.125
It was my choice to help you.

11:08.209 --> 11:09.585
This isn't your fault.

11:10.169 --> 11:12.421
Gosha was worried too.

11:12.505 --> 11:14.340
You told my grandfather?

11:14.423 --> 11:17.635
I did. He sure let me have it.

11:19.095 --> 11:21.597
I can't involve you in this anymore.

11:21.680 --> 11:24.141
- But...
- That's the end of it.

11:24.809 --> 11:25.851
No, it isn't.

11:26.352 --> 11:27.937
It's not finished yet for me.

11:28.562 --> 11:31.857
I want to talk to Melon again,
just one more time.

11:32.733 --> 11:35.778
If you have any information about him,
please tell me.

11:41.742 --> 11:43.327
We've got nothing right now.

11:43.411 --> 11:45.037
I see.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.623
Besides, what good
would talking to him do?

11:47.706 --> 11:49.583
We can't know unless we try.

11:50.167 --> 11:52.211
I'll do it myself!

11:53.629 --> 11:54.713
Hey!

12:01.262 --> 12:06.308
Number 10, number 11, number 12.

12:08.018 --> 12:10.604
All right. Next, the spotlight.

12:13.983 --> 12:16.610
Hey! What are you doing in here?

12:17.361 --> 12:21.824
Are Cosmo and Luna here?

12:21.907 --> 12:24.702
What do you need them for?

12:25.202 --> 12:27.746
Forget it. They're not coming back.

12:28.581 --> 12:31.292
PERFORMANCE CANCELED

12:31.375 --> 12:36.213
So... About the organizer of that party...

12:36.297 --> 12:38.090
Go home, son.

12:38.174 --> 12:41.218
Any information will help.

12:41.719 --> 12:43.596
Huh? Your tail...

12:44.763 --> 12:46.015
It's nothing.

12:46.098 --> 12:48.934
- Get out of here, you pest.
- I won't bother you.

12:49.018 --> 12:52.354
Don't you get it?
You already are bothering me!

12:53.063 --> 12:56.442
My best dancers gone.
My tail cut clean off.

12:58.611 --> 13:00.946
<i>Don't say anything
about the investigation.</i>

13:01.030 --> 13:02.781
<i>It'll put the girls in danger, too.</i>

13:04.658 --> 13:05.659
<i>Oh, no.</i>

13:06.744 --> 13:10.789
Forgive me. I'm so sorry. I'll leave now.

13:13.125 --> 13:16.462
- Just one thing before I go.
- Get out of here!

13:16.545 --> 13:18.881
The third one from the back is out.

13:18.964 --> 13:19.965
What?

13:20.466 --> 13:21.926
I'm sorry for the trouble.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.136
You're right.

13:27.223 --> 13:29.058
A strange pattern...

13:30.267 --> 13:35.481
Cosmo said something about seeing
a strange pattern through his shirt.

13:37.024 --> 13:38.275
A strange pattern?

13:45.491 --> 13:47.284
<i>A strange pattern?</i>

13:48.410 --> 13:49.620
<i>What could that mean?</i>

13:54.124 --> 13:55.251
What are you looking at?

14:00.756 --> 14:04.593
Marine creatures don't understand
this wonderful feeling.

14:04.677 --> 14:06.428
What a shame.

14:07.137 --> 14:09.014
So, you like baths now?

14:09.098 --> 14:11.725
Yes, finally.

14:11.809 --> 14:13.644
You weren't into it at first.

14:14.603 --> 14:15.854
That's right.

14:16.647 --> 14:19.441
I like coming with you.

14:19.525 --> 14:21.610
Everyone's naked.

14:21.694 --> 14:26.740
Land animals wear clothing
to protect themselves.

14:26.824 --> 14:29.910
But in the bath, they're naked.

14:29.994 --> 14:32.496
It's like we're
shedding the constraints of society...

14:32.997 --> 14:34.039
Or something.

14:34.123 --> 14:35.624
Constraints?

14:35.708 --> 14:39.003
When you took your clothes off,
I could see your scars.

14:39.086 --> 14:42.339
Oh, these? A lot has happened.

14:42.840 --> 14:43.674
A lot?

14:46.093 --> 14:50.222
Eating good food, soaking in the bath.

14:50.306 --> 14:52.308
That's what really makes me feel alive.

14:53.851 --> 14:56.896
Don't cry! I'm all right!

14:58.022 --> 15:00.649
I'm not crying. It's the water.

15:00.733 --> 15:01.734
The water?

15:02.318 --> 15:05.112
I've never cried
in the ocean before, either.

15:05.195 --> 15:08.949
In the ocean, dying is nothing.

15:09.033 --> 15:11.869
I don't cry when my friends die.

15:12.578 --> 15:13.829
But...

15:13.913 --> 15:18.292
I don't want my friend Legoshi to die.

15:18.792 --> 15:21.003
On land, I'd cry for you.

15:21.086 --> 15:22.671
Sagwan...

15:23.589 --> 15:28.636
Legoshi.
If you're ever in trouble in the ocean,

15:28.719 --> 15:29.929
scream like this.

15:34.141 --> 15:35.142
What are you doing?

15:46.862 --> 15:47.947
What does that mean?

15:48.447 --> 15:52.159
It means, "I am Legoshi the Gray Wolf."

15:52.701 --> 15:54.870
Next, the magic words.

16:05.673 --> 16:06.840
What did you say?

16:07.508 --> 16:08.384
It's a secret.

16:09.760 --> 16:10.761
Tell me!

16:11.845 --> 16:13.555
BATH HOUSE

16:13.639 --> 16:16.725
Come on, Sagwan. Tell me.

16:19.228 --> 16:20.312
What did that mean?

16:22.648 --> 16:24.149
Something smells good.

16:25.275 --> 16:27.027
You're right.

16:27.111 --> 16:28.862
Wait, don't change the subject!

16:29.530 --> 16:30.531
Welcome!

16:31.156 --> 16:32.241
Two, please.

16:32.324 --> 16:33.158
OCTOPUS

16:33.242 --> 16:35.452
<i>- Catching sea creatures...</i>
- Sure.

16:35.536 --> 16:37.079
- That'll be 600 yen.
<i>- That's illegal.</i>

16:37.162 --> 16:42.918
Oh, but since you're a sea creature,
I'll only charge you 650 yen!

16:43.460 --> 16:44.753
Thank you.

16:45.838 --> 16:48.757
Sagwan, what are you doing? This is wrong!

16:48.841 --> 16:50.634
It's fine.

16:51.093 --> 16:52.261
Here you are.

16:53.762 --> 16:55.389
Six hundred yen, right?

16:56.140 --> 16:58.434
This looks so good.

17:01.103 --> 17:03.272
Stop it! You can't!

17:03.355 --> 17:05.190
Those are your fellow sea creatures!

17:07.192 --> 17:09.153
Have you forgotten, Legoshi?

17:09.236 --> 17:14.950
In the ocean, we eat and are eaten.
That's our normal life.

17:16.994 --> 17:20.372
You did say that. But...

17:20.456 --> 17:21.665
They're dead now.

17:22.207 --> 17:25.127
It's too late. They aren't coming back.

17:31.050 --> 17:32.509
<i>The food chain.</i>

17:33.677 --> 17:35.721
<i>Logically, I understand it,</i>

17:35.804 --> 17:39.850
<i>but when I see it before my own eyes,
it doesn't feel right.</i>

17:41.351 --> 17:43.062
That sure was tasty!

17:44.480 --> 17:50.402
It's better that I eat them
rather than some mysterious land creature,

17:50.486 --> 17:53.739
isn't it, Legoshi?

17:54.573 --> 17:55.866
Sure.

17:55.949 --> 17:59.536
You're kind, Legoshi. Too kind.

18:01.163 --> 18:03.665
Delicious food is delicious.

18:03.749 --> 18:05.584
Just like udon.

18:05.667 --> 18:08.212
Udon isn't a living thing.

18:08.796 --> 18:10.923
Thanks for the food.

18:11.924 --> 18:14.093
Poaching is a crime.

18:15.928 --> 18:17.638
Come on, Sagwan. Let's go.

18:18.263 --> 18:20.808
You just said it was delicious!
What's wrong with you?

18:21.475 --> 18:24.311
I wonder what kind of sensation
"delicious" is.

18:27.272 --> 18:28.649
I'll take one.

18:28.732 --> 18:30.109
Sure. That'll be 400 yen.

18:37.366 --> 18:42.621
<i>I don't have the sense of taste
of either an herbivore or a carnivore.</i>

18:43.539 --> 18:46.250
<i>No matter how rich the flavor,</i>

18:46.333 --> 18:48.877
<i>no matter what the food is,</i>

18:49.461 --> 18:53.048
<i>it all tastes like sand to me.</i>

18:58.804 --> 19:01.974
<i>I have no appetite or sexual desire.</i>

19:02.057 --> 19:07.146
<i>I have no one
to expose my face or body to.</i>

19:07.271 --> 19:10.858
<i>This is the only place I can find peace.</i>

19:10.941 --> 19:13.485
THE BLUE DRAGON

19:13.569 --> 19:15.571
Hello, Melon!

19:15.654 --> 19:17.072
Is he here?

19:18.115 --> 19:21.076
He sent another customer to the hospital.

19:22.035 --> 19:25.706
I fired him, but he's still working away.

19:26.999 --> 19:28.834
Yo, Holger.

19:32.921 --> 19:37.301
Calling you a psycho-killer, how absurd.

19:37.384 --> 19:41.805
You're just too slow to realize
your victims are bleeding out.

19:42.472 --> 19:43.974
Yeah.

19:45.184 --> 19:49.980
- Aren't you going to welcome me?
- Wel...

19:50.063 --> 19:53.859
come...

19:57.654 --> 19:59.573
Look at this.

19:59.698 --> 20:03.327
My leopard spots
have spread all the way to here.

20:06.371 --> 20:09.833
Turn them into melon leaves, as usual.

20:09.917 --> 20:12.711
Cultivate my melon field for me.

20:15.589 --> 20:18.342
NIMBLE

20:29.186 --> 20:31.104
Yes. That's the spot.

20:31.647 --> 20:34.149
How I love this feeling.

20:36.610 --> 20:37.736
Pure pleasure.

20:41.073 --> 20:43.825
Pain is the only thing
that makes me feel alive.

20:45.077 --> 20:46.995
What's going to happen to me?

20:47.079 --> 20:51.291
Will I become a leopard?

21:08.725 --> 21:10.060
THE BLUE DRAGON

21:11.603 --> 21:13.146
Hello?

21:31.123 --> 21:32.374
<i>Am I too late?</i>

21:37.170 --> 21:39.715
Sorry, I didn't hear you come in!

21:39.798 --> 21:42.467
Oh, this? Don't worry,
it's not like anyone was murdered.

21:42.968 --> 21:45.762
Our last customer just bled a lot.

21:45.846 --> 21:50.100
Gun... Dangerous...

21:50.934 --> 21:52.185
Gun?

21:52.269 --> 21:54.229
Don't listen to him. This guy...

21:54.313 --> 21:57.816
- He's still talking to his last customer.
- Put it...

21:57.899 --> 22:00.444
away...

22:00.527 --> 22:03.488
Melon.

22:04.656 --> 22:07.659
<i>He's talking to Melon?</i>

22:09.244 --> 22:10.620
<i>I might be on to something.</i>

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
